# The gallery is generated, not written: scripts/capture-gallery.py drives the
# running app and REPLACES both files wholesale. Two branches that each
# re-captured therefore have no meaningful three-way merge — line-level
# resolution would interleave two different capture runs into a document that
# never existed and that docs/audit.js would happily pass. `-merge` makes git
# stop and say so instead, and the resolution is always the same: re-capture.
#
# `-diff linguist-generated=true` keeps a 400KB machine-written blob out of
# review diffs, where it is noise around whatever the change actually was.
docs/gallery-states.json -merge -diff linguist-generated=true
docs/style-gallery.html  -merge -diff linguist-generated=true
